## Candidate-survival and omission audit

### Modeled OAV < 1 survival dispositions

Fresh pipeline pending. Replace with the exact modeled set before verification.

### Takeover, redundancy, adaptation, and stock-rebase audit

Coriander and cardamom share linalool/terpinyl continuity but remain a takeover risk, so their ratio is isolated below. Aromatic stacking is bounded to one lavender natural plus Clary Sage; juniper, pine, rosemary, spike lavender and Calone are excluded. The two literal cedars are shaped by vetiver and Sandalore rather than a prestige amberwood wall. Givaudan AIMI exact stock-specific OAV is DATA HOLD. Natural OAV is composite and diagnostic only.

## Inventory and stock audit

All current rows resolve against live inventory and avoid Polysantol, Ambrofix, Bacdanol and Guaiacwood EO 33%. Romandolide is the sole exact musk. No stock substitution or sensory equivalence is inferred.

## Working-stock preparation ledger

- `Aldehyde C10` — owned 1% stock, 20 uL. Carrier is unverified; use only the labeled stock and HOLD a physical carrier-matched omission until verified.
- `Aldehyde C11` — owned 1% stock, 20 uL. Carrier is unverified; use only the labeled stock and HOLD a physical carrier-matched omission until verified.
- `Suederal` — owned 10% stock, 30 uL. Carrier is unverified; use only the labeled stock and HOLD a physical carrier-matched omission until verified.
- `Tonkarome` — owned 20% w/w in TEC, 200 uL nominal-volume design dose. Use the labeled stock; a matched omission replaces 200 uL with TEC.
- `Tonka Bean Absolute` — owned 10% in DPG, basis unspecified, 100 uL nominal-volume design dose. Use the labeled stock; a matched omission replaces 100 uL with DPG.

No direct dose is below 10 uL. Unknown-carrier stocks are used only as labeled whole stocks; matched physical omission arms remain HOLD until carrier verification.

## Missing-chemical impact gate

Polysantol and Parmavert remain ideal lineage but unavailable in the current build. Sandalore and molecular violet materials are target-native architecture, not equivalents. Missing coriander CO2, lavender absolute and Haitian vetiver reduce oily seed depth, hayed lavender interior and lifted root nuance as design-risk hypotheses. Sensory consequences remain NOT TESTED/HOLD.

## Future mixing order

NOT AUTHORIZED. If later authorized: verify stocks and controls; combine adhesion and Romandolide; build cedar/vetiver and pressure rails; add violet cloth and stitches; fold in lavender silk; add coriander/cardamom shell; finish with green sparkle.

## Controlled blinded test plan

Use two independently prepared complete sets, anonymous codes, counterbalanced AB/BA order and free description before scoring. Compare V8 with LN-01 at 0, 5, 30 and 120 minutes, 6 hours and 24 hours. Score overall liking, transition pleasure, drydown pleasure, re-smell desire, target continuity, seed integration, lavender restraint, violet-to-wood connection, takeover defects and fatigue separately.

**Cardamom/coriander causal isolation:** prepare constant-total, carrier-matched A=current, B=coriander omission with 220 uL matched neutral matrix, C=cardamom low at 130 uL plus 130 uL matched matrix, and D=both changes. Use D - B - C + A only as an interaction estimate, never proof of synergy. Natural-stock density and safety remain HOLD.

